# Item 739, its result side: at the root a held callable whose header result is not int --
# `fn: (size_t: x) size_t` here -- is called through l2_mad_call's size_t variant, which hands the
# walk a size_t cell (the walk reads a destination it did not classify as an int).  Before, the
# header was refused, located ("a held callable whose result is not int"); before that row, the
# root wrapped the int-typed value in an int -> size_t edge and the walk failed at run time.
# add5: 1 is 6.  Mutant: every held call through l2_mad_call (int) -- walk error: INVALID.
fn: makeAdder (size_t: n) fn: (size_t: x) size_t
    fn: addN (size_t: x) size_t
        return: x + n
    return: addN

add5: makeAdder 5U
size_t: a (add5: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 6U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
